\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces What the data say about $\kappa $, on the simplex of three genes; schematic, with compositions chosen for legibility. With the neighbours' influx $\bar  {\bm  {\rho }}_i$ held fixed, each $\kappa $ implies the clean composition $\bm  {\rho }_i(\kappa ) = (\mathbf  {p}_i - \kappa \bar  {\bm  {\rho }}_i)/(1-\kappa )$: a line that starts at the observed composition $\mathbf  {p}_i$ ($\kappa = 0$) and runs away from $\bar  {\bm  {\rho }}_i$ (arrow). It is valid until it leaves the simplex at $\bar  \kappa _i$ (diamond) and invalid beyond (dashed). \textbf  {a},\nobreakspace  {}A cell that expresses a little of the neighbours' marker itself: every $\kappa \in [0, \bar  \kappa _i]$ reproduces $\mathbf  {p}_i$ exactly, and the true value lies inside. \textbf  {b},\nobreakspace  {}A cell that cannot express the marker: its true composition lies on the edge, the line leaves the simplex exactly there, and $\bar  \kappa _i$ is the true $\kappa $.\relax }}{25}{figure.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kappa-bound}{{7}{25}{What the data say about $\kappa $, on the simplex of three genes; schematic, with compositions chosen for legibility. With the neighbours' influx $\rhobar _i$ held fixed, each $\kappa $ implies the clean composition $\vrho _i(\kappa ) = (\vp _i - \kappa \rhobar _i)/(1-\kappa )$: a line that starts at the observed composition $\vp _i$ ($\kappa = 0$) and runs away from $\rhobar _i$ (arrow). It is valid until it leaves the simplex at $\bar \kappa _i$ (diamond) and invalid beyond (dashed). \textbf {a},~A cell that expresses a little of the neighbours' marker itself: every $\kappa \in [0, \bar \kappa _i]$ reproduces $\vp _i$ exactly, and the true value lies inside. \textbf {b},~A cell that cannot express the marker: its true composition lies on the edge, the line leaves the simplex exactly there, and $\bar \kappa _i$ is the true $\kappa $.\relax }{figure.caption.38}{}}
\newlabel{fig:kappa-bound@cref}{{[figure][7][2147483647]7}{[1][23][]25}}
